group features/cli
note group-rename <old> <new>: move every tour in group old, and in every group nested inside it, to the same place under new. The agent reaches for it to reorganise a whole branch of the map in one move instead of regrouping every tour in it (commit 10dc7e690b8b). An empty new moves them to the top level. Since a group exists only as a name on its tours, renaming is rewriting that name on each tour; it fails when no tour is in old.

